.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt LICENSE_HEADERS.SH 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm license_headers.sh
.Nd add or remove copyright and license headers on source files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a | Fl -add
.Op Fl r | Fl -remove-all
.Op Fl h | Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is an optional POSIX-compliant script that adds or removes a standard copyright and license header on every
.Pa .c
and
.Pa .h
file under
.Pa src/ .
.Pp
Must be invoked from the project root.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a , Fl -add
Add the header to files that don't already have it.
This is the default behavior when no mode flag is given.
.It Fl r , Fl -remove-all
Remove the header from files where it exactly matches the
header defined in the script.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show the help message and exit.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
\&./scripts/license_headers.sh              # Add headers where missing
\&./scripts/license_headers.sh --add        # Same as above, explicit
\&./scripts/license_headers.sh --remove-all # Remove headers where present
.Ed
.Sh TRICKS & TIPS
After this script successfully completes, run
.Pp
.Dl ./build --lint
.Pp
to verify formatting and confirm all license-header checks pass.
.Pp
To modify the copyright or license text itself, first remove all
existing headers with
.Fl -remove-all ,
edit the header definition within the script, then re-run with
.Fl -add .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr build.sh 1 ,
.Xr install.sh 1 ,
.Xr install_man.sh 1 ,
.Xr uninstall.sh 1
